    "bodyDigest": "sha256:22101d7c80335af81ac2d86ac0220b6bc8f04cb88773be0702dda554eb6231e1",
    "bodySummary": "Outcome: 🟢 已声明的验证通过 — WI-1083-windows-receipt-store-pin-proof",
    "deliveryId": "sha256:a446226190c9d94c37fc2a10a3b9bcb22cabdb851e7bb18c570b73e96118bf6d",
    "deliveryState": "returned_to_consumer",
    "hostConfirmation": "unknown",
    "language": "zh",
    "legacyOutcome": {
      "acceptanceResults": [
        "Only crates/cockpit-repository/tests/receipt_store.rs and Windows test-only content in crates/cockpit-repository/src/evidence_store.rs change; production non-test behavior and statements, public API, dependencies and workflow remain unchanged. Preserve WI-1081/WI-1082 worktrees and archive records.",
        "After persist_reusable_receipt successfully opens index.lock and before lock.lock, a cfg(all(test,windows))-only worker-thread-local one-shot ready/resume hook binds the actual opened directory and lock identities. The event states that handles are open but the lock has not been acquired. Run the original persist implementation; do not copy writes or use 100ms sleep as proof.",
        "Move only the Windows timing-sensitive scenario to private library unit tests; keep all other integration scenarios and preserve or strengthen every original rename-success sentinel/no replacement index/restore/readback safety assertion. No generic test framework or public test-support API.",
        "For a failed rename require unchanged original directory volume/file identity and path, absent destination/replacement, then resume/unlock/join and exact first+second receipt readback with complete index, node/repository/profile/receipt ID bindings and no redirection. Only after all proof succeeds may raw Windows errno5 or32 be accepted; every other errno or failed assertion fails.",
        "Explicitly drop the fixture main-thread lock File and temporary identity handles as needed; unlocking is not handle release. After all handles are released require successful rename on the same path as a positive control. The test must not keep extra no-delete directory handles that manufacture the expected refusal.",
        "Use bounded per-worker ready/resume synchronization and panic-safe worker release/join. Native Windows --lib execution must select the exact scoped test with a nonzero count; Linux cfg exclusion or zero tests is not Windows acceptance. Existing CI repository --lib is unchanged; a dedicated one-case native test subprocess is allowed if needed to expose exact-selection evidence without workflow changes.",
        "Preserve original failed CI38649495827 at source00e89d21d6a00d09819f8353ae0a1391b954f171, Windows job116146092900, receipt_store.rs322 actualerrno5 expected32. Do not use WI-1082 green to overwrite it. Distinguish deterministic assertion-model RED/GREEN from already-correct production behavior and do not force a kernel error race.",
        "Run the targeted assertion matrix, related receipt_store integration and complete cargo test --workspace --all-targets through fresh Runtime admission, with an isolated target, one build job, writable HOME/TMPDIR and a 900-second host cap. Obtain real Windows-native exact-case and integration results through CI; preserve raw commands and receipts.",
        "Use an independent ordinary Work Item at exact fetched main00461714bd43d3f6c42ede66491e01d22d475604, with its own branch/worktree. Raydot approved independent admission without waiting for WI-1082 human close. Timely commit/push an independent Draft PR for source/evidence review; do not merge, delete, perform human close or system/environment redesign."
      ],
